    <h1>A1.1.8 – Data Compression</h1>

    <h2>📌 Learning Objective</h2>
    <p>By the end of this lesson, you will be able to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Describe</strong> the concept of compression and why it is used (storage space, transmission time, bandwidth)</li>
        <li><strong>Describe</strong> the difference between lossy and lossless compression methods, including when each is appropriate</li>
        <li><strong>Describe</strong> how Run-Length Encoding (RLE) and transform coding work, giving for each the technology, a defining characteristic, and a typical use</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🎯 IB Command Term: <span class="badge">Describe</span></h2>
    <div class="command-term">
        <strong>Describe</strong> – <em>"Give a detailed account."</em><br><br>
        Simply naming a compression method (e.g., "JPEG") is not describing it. This lesson builds the skill of providing a detailed account of how compression works, what it achieves, and the trade-offs involved.
    </div>

